        "title": "feat(mac): redesign menu bar icon as crisp lens-ghost template",
        "body": "## Before / After\n\n<img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/openclaw/Peekaboo/f271b453ee92b62c5f63891c14d699f112440df2/.github/pr-assets/menubar-icon-before-after.png\" width=\"560\" alt=\"Before and after comparison of the menu bar icon on light and dark menubar backgrounds\">\n\n## Summary\n\nRedesigns the macOS menu bar icon as a clean, vector-rendered template ghost with a camera-lens belly that echoes the app icon's identity.\n\nBefore: a crude 18px cartoon-ghost bitmap where the 2x and 3x asset files were byte-identical copies of the same 36px image, so the icon rendered blurry on Retina displays.\n\nAfter:\n- New ghost silhouette (smooth dome, wavy three-lobe hem, cut-out eyes) with an aperture-style lens ring in the belly, matching the app icon's ghost-with-lens mark.\n- Rendered from a single CoreGraphics path at true 1x/2x/3x (18/36/54 px), so it is pixel-crisp on all displays.\n- The imageset is now marked `template-rendering-intent: template` in the asset catalog (previously only enforced in code).\n- Removed `GhostMenuIcon.swift`, an unused programmatic icon drawer with zero references.\n\nAll consumers (`StatusBarController`, `MenuBarAnimationController`, settings header views) load the `MenuIcon` asset by name and pick up the new art with no code changes.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `./scripts/build-mac-debug.sh` builds green.\n- Verified via `assetutil --info` that the compiled `Assets.car` contains the new 1x/2x/3x renditions.\n- Confirmed `GhostMenuIcon` had no references outside its own file before deletion.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
